//! Stage runtime: the BG manager, the BG scene and the course-file parser.
//!
//! ## What this module covers
//!
//! `main.dol` code that turns an archive handle into the background resources a
//! course needs, plus the course-file parser that fills the stage object. The
//! original addresses are `0x80081070..0x800826E0`, `0x80083380..0x80083BD0`
//! (BG-unit model) and `0x8008D3D0..0x8008EBE0` (camera edges, spatial list and
//! course-section accessors):
//!
//! | address | name here | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x80081070` | [`bg_manager_construct`] | zero the 0x328-byte BG manager and install its vtable |
//! | `0x800813F0` | [`unit_name`] | address of one inline BG-unit name |
//! | `0x80081410` | [`copy_unit_names`] | copy four unit names per stage into the manager |
//! | `0x800814D0` | [`load_bg_units`] | load the three bgdat layers and the BG-unit files |
//! | `0x800816A0` | [`create_bg_unit_models`] | create three BG-unit models per stage |
//! | `0x80081780` | [`refresh_bg_unit_models`] | rebuild those models after a layer change |
//! | `0x80081800` | [`init_stage_resources`] | entry point: archive → names → layers → models |
//! | `0x80081850` | [`bg_unit_model`] | model-handle accessor (`+0x34`) |
//! | `0x80081870` | [`bg_unit_u16`] | `u16` read through the `+0x64` texture block |
//! | `0x80081890` | [`bg_unit_mesh_offset`] | `+0xA4` mesh base plus a byte offset |
//! | `0x80081BE0` | [`is_current_stage_unit`] | world/stage/area compare against stage info |
//! | `0x80081C40` | [`bg_scene_camera_entry`] | pick a stage entry from the camera position |
//! | `0x80081D20` | [`create_bg_scene`] | BG scene constructor (partial) |
//! | `0x80081F40` | [`alloc_tile_buffers`] | allocate and zero 12 × 64 KiB tile buffers |
//! | `0x80082050` | [`free_tile_buffers`] | free every tile buffer of a scene |
//! | `0x800820D0` | [`free_tile_buffer`] | free one tile buffer and null its slot |
//! | `0x80082160` | [`bg_scene_clear`] | clear the four dwords at `+0x84` |
//! | `0x80082180` | [`bg_scene_update_x_direction`] | classify scene origin x against the camera |
//! | `0x800821E0` | [`bg_scene_update_z_direction`] | classify scene origin z against the camera |
//! | `0x80082240` | [`bg_scene_wrap_x`] | wrap an x coordinate across the stage width |
//! | `0x80082310` | [`bg_tilemap_construct`] | construct the 0x44-byte BG tile-map object |
//! | `0x80082410` | [`bg_tilemap_init`] | fill a tile map's two per-cell arrays |
//! | `0x80082560` | [`bg_tilemap_release`] | release the two arrays and the attached buffer |
//! | `0x800826C0` | [`bg_tilemap_set`] | write one tile value into a tile map |
//! | `0x800826E0` | [`bg_scene_camera_limits`] | current camera x/z wrap limits |
//! | `0x8008DFF0` | [`parse_course_file`] | parse `course/course<N>.bin` into a stage object |
//! | `0x80083380` | [`bg_tilemap_set_at`] | write a tile by absolute coordinate, returning the old value |
//! | `0x80083560` | [`bg_unit_model_create`] | allocate or refresh a BG-unit model |
//! | `0x80083660` | [`bg_unit_model_clear`] | clear the model's tile-id and pointer tables |
//! | `0x800837D0` | [`bg_unit_model_alloc_palette`] | allocate and fill one 256-entry palette block |
//! | `0x80083AD0` | [`bg_unit_model_bind_heap`] | attach or swap the model's buffer heap |
//! | `0x80083B40` | [`bg_unit_model_tile_at`] | locate one 2-byte tile cell in a model |
//! | `0x80083BD0` | [`bg_unit_model_resolve_names`] | resolve three unit-name strings to table indices |
//! | `0x80083F90` | [`bg_unit_model_tile_index`] | map a world tile coordinate to a tile-table index |
//! | `0x8008D3D0` | [`segment_side_x`] | side of an x-ordered 2-D segment |
//! | `0x8008D820` | [`segment_side_y`] | side of a y-ordered 2-D segment |
//! | `0x8008DCF0` | [`spatial_list_release`] | free every entry of the 0x1C-byte list |
//! | `0x8008DDB0` | [`spatial_entry_store`] | insert or update a position-keyed list entry |
//! | `0x8008E530` | [`section4b_byte_e`] | byte `+0xE` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E560` | [`section4b_byte_f`] | byte `+0xF` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E590` | [`section4b_byte_10`] | byte `+0x10` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E5C0` | [`section4b_byte_16`] | byte `+0x16` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E5F0` | [`section4b_byte_17`] | byte `+0x17` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E620` | [`section4b_byte_11`] | byte `+0x11` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E6B0` | [`section4b_u16_8`] | `u16` at `+8` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E710` | [`section4b_byte_14`] | byte `+0x14` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E740` | [`section4b_u16_4`] | `u16` at `+4` of a section-4B entry |
//! | `0x8008E950` | [`rect_contains_point`] | point-in-rectangle test with the 0x80 margin |
//! | `0x8008EA20` | [`rect_overlaps`] | centre-distance rectangle overlap test |
//! | `0x8008EAF0` | [`section5b_entry_by_index`] | `0x14`-byte section-5B entry by index |
//! | `0x8008EBE0` | [`stage_objects_release`] | destroy and free the four stage objects |
//!
//! The wave-5 batch continues in three adjacent clusters, all still in this
//! file: the 2-D collision-area object (`0x8008C200..0x8008CA50`), the
//! stage-slot record used while a course changes (`0x8008EBA0..0x8008F000`),
//! and the BG-unit tile/palette helpers (`0x800833E0..0x80083EE0`). The public
//! entry points are [`collision_area_overlap`], [`collision_area_resolve`],
//! [`stage_slot_refresh`] and [`bg_unit_tile_probe`]; the full address table is
//! in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE5_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-7 batch finally lands that pending pair of clusters, one cluster
//! at a time: the BG-unit tile-selection helpers
//! (`0x80085E40..0x80086FE0`, the code that turns a tile command into a tile
//! id and writes it back into the model) and the dynamic-library (dDyl)
//! resource slots that bring stage RELs in while a course changes
//! (`0x8008F110..0x8008F870`). Those two clusters are listed in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE7_STAGE.md`. The dDyl slot is a separate 0x14-byte
//! object from the 0x34-byte stage-slot record above: it holds a loader
//! handle, not a course id. Wave 7 also adds the camera depth selectors
//! (`0x800872E0..0x80087360`), the stage animation list
//! (`0x80087890..0x80087C30`) and three stage helpers
//! (`0x80088D90..0x80089030`).
//!
//! The wave-10 batch continues into the next main.dol band
//! (`0x800A0000..0x80100000`): the course manager that owns the stage slots
//! (`0x800BB090..0x800BBC90`), the camera globals behind `bg_camera_*`
//! (`0x800CD230..0x800CD3E0`), the stage-object section lookups
//! (`0x800CD470..0x800D90C0`) and the stage-resource readiness test
//! (`0x800E3640..0x800E3AB0`). The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE10_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-15 batch fills the remaining stage gaps in
//! `0x80083D00..0x800919A0`: the BG tile-command pipeline
//! (`0x80083D00`, `0x80085780`, `0x800859F0`, `0x80086D10`), the BG texture
//! manager and animation list (`0x80087380..0x80087B60`), the stage environment
//! object (`0x80088CF0..0x80089DC0`), the dDyl stage-resource table
//! (`0x8008F460..0x8008F760`) and the stage block object
//! (`0x80090590..0x800919A0`). The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE15_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-18 batch returns to the lower part of the band
//! (`0x80080170..0x8008FCD0`): the BG-scene scroll-layer lists and predicates
//! (`0x80080170..0x80081030`), the stage camera object and its two GX
//! submission helpers (`0x80089ED0..0x8008A280`), the stage-block fill/coin
//! model helpers and the two render-mode initialisers
//! (`0x8008A8E0..0x8008BA00`), and the dDyl resource-path wrappers
//! (`0x8008F810..0x8008FCD0`). The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE18_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-103 batch closes part of the `0x80070000` band: the contact-query
//! family (`0x80073290`, `0x80073BC0`, `0x80073670`), the cell-walk pair
//! (`0x80070130`, `0x80071A60`), the slide and terrain updates (`0x80071210`,
//! `0x8007E4E0`) and the BG tile-decode pair (`0x80077730`, `0x80077810`).
//! Nine bodies, 6260 bytes; the remaining sixteen entries are listed with
//! their reasons in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE103_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-104 batch closes fourteen of the twenty-three open entries of the
//! `0x800B0000` bucket: the four lift-grid writers [`fn_800be000`]
//! (`0x800BE000`), [`fn_800bd7a0`] (`0x800BD7A0`), [`fn_800be390`]
//! (`0x800BE390`) and [`fn_800bf3f0`] (`0x800BF3F0`); the four sprite-node
