//! [`fn_80078250`], [`fn_8007d5b0`] and [`fn_800713b0`]. The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE83_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-84 batch closes the last untranslated gaps of the `0x8009xxxx`
//! actor band that wave 69 opened: the `Wm` sub-actor ground/owner helpers
//! (`0x80097700..0x80097F70`, the two-float ground query, the player-owner scan,
//! the cached-position refresh, the `0x269` effect submit and the variant
//! record publisher), the course-actor subclass with its seven shared
//! type-info stubs, constructor, two destructors, refresh pass and frame
//! driver (`0x80098350..0x80098D90`), and the eight motion/effect helpers
//! `0x8009B980..0x8009BFE0`, plus the duplicated `0x802DCBFC` forwarding pair
//! at `0x8009AC40`/`0x8009AC70`. The subclass keeps its vtable at `+0x60`, its
//! `0x5FC`-byte state (`+0x524` list, `+0x544` motion object, `+0x5A8..+0x5B4`
//! vector, `+0x5F0..+0x5F8` tail) and its `+0x414..+0x432` variant record. The
//! seven 12-byte stubs all return the shared type-info record `0x80377A04`.
//! The full table is in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE84_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-85 batch fills four untranslated runs of the `0x800Cxxxx` band
//! between the dLineMng and dMaskMng waves: the lift-actor model and cell code
//! (`0x800C0310..0x800C0D70`, the `lift_han_*` model/palette constructors, the
//! `0x44`-byte cell position/palette writers and the two release wrappers), the
//! lift interpolation reset (`0x800C1810`), the cave/mask record cluster
//! (`0x800CAA10..0x800CB1C0`, the state override, the `cave_bti` load and the
//! four strip objects) and the message/mask tail
//! (`0x800CBF60..0x800CE020`, the two auxiliary mask objects with their render
//! binders, the mask row record and its two release wrappers, the mask refresh
//! pass, and the three message accessors). The cell table is `0x80164B60` with
//! its count at `+0`, records at `+4` (stride `0x44`), palette at `+8` and flags
//! at `+4`; the lift model tables are `0x80316708`/`0x803167C8`/`0x80316940`.
//! The public entry points are [`fn_800c0310`], [`fn_800c0bf0`],
//! [`fn_800caa10`] and [`fn_800ccd90`]. The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE85_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-88 batch returns to the `0x800Bxxxx` course-manager band and fills
//! five untranslated runs that wave 75 left around its actor-list and node-list
//! work: the message/slot prompt helpers (`0x800B4DE0..0x800B54C0`), the
//! element block/instance wrappers and the two teardown chains
//! (`0x800B6BE0..0x800B7DB0`), the element passes that walk the `+0x88`-linked
//! node list (`0x800BA240..0x800BB010`), the kanaami strip constructor and its
//! two placement helpers (`0x800BBD30`/`0x800BBDD0`, `0x800BCA40`/
//! `0x800BCB80`), and the panel-grid draw helpers
//! (`0x800BE340..0x800BE930`). The node list is the one wave 75 described
//! (`+0x1C` count, `+0x20` head, `+0x88` next pointer); this pass adds the
//! per-node `+0x24` source record and the two `0x28`-byte interface
//! sub-objects whose `+0x18` slot takes the `0x80358C18`/`0x80358D18`
//! descriptors. The public entry points are [`fn_800b4de0`],
//! [`fn_800ba480`], [`fn_800bb010`] and [`fn_800be7b0`]. The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE88_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-91 batch returns to the `0x8007xxxx` BG scene band and lands five
//! contiguous clusters that wave 83 only touched at their edges: the three
//! trigger-record decoders (`0x80072DB0..0x80073070`), the two angle-scan
//! wrappers (`0x80073B40`/`0x800743D0`), the scene constructor with its
//! cell-probe helpers (`0x80077060..0x80077B00`), the seven per-mode aspect-fit
//! selectors (`0x80078860..0x800795E0`) and the draw/clamp tail
//! (`0x8007AB70..0x8007FB10`). Those bodies are the first to name the `r2`
//! constant block at `0x8042BC40..0x8042BE2C` (the `4096.0f` fixed-point scale,
//! the `2^52 + 2^31` signed-int bias and the fit ratios) and the three
//! `0x802EF6xx..0x802EF8xx` float tables. The public entry points are
//! [`fn_80077060`] (scene constructor), [`fn_8007e860`] (visible-cell pass) and
//! [`fn_800791d0`] (scene scale). The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE91_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-92 batch closes the next untranslated stretch of the same
//! `0x8009xxxx` actor band, `0x8009BA70..0x8009F770`: the animation-id binder
//! and the two-value predicate of the `Wm_jr` subclass
//! (`0x8009BA70`/`0x8009BCE0`), the seven spin/land/jump/break effect helpers
//! (`0x8009C350..0x8009CA30`), the clown damage/squat/fire actions
//! (`0x8009D010..0x8009D540`), the delete helpers, parent-chain walkers and
//! path comparisons they share with wave 69 (`0x8009E6D0..0x8009ED10`) and the
//! `+0x1080` model-state family (`0x8009F250..0x8009F770`). The bodies keep the
//! wave-69 field vocabulary (`+0x30` parent link, `+0x60` vtable,
//! `+0x348`/`+0x38D` variant/player bytes, `+0x414..+0x432` variant record) and
