//! `+0x600`/`+0x604`/`+0x644` clown animation triple. The public entry points
//! are [`fn_8009c350`], [`fn_8009d540`], [`fn_8009e830`] and [`fn_8009f5f0`].
//! The full table is in `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE92_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-93 batch closes the `0x800C0000` functions that do not depend on
//! the paired-single math chain: the lift-arm
//! initialiser (`0x800C10F0`, the only writer of the `+0x38..+0x69` half of
//! the block [`fn_800c1810`] clears), the message formatter and archive mount
//! (`0x800C9E80`, `0x800CDB30`, `0x800CDC70`), the character model
//! constructor/destructor pair (`0x800CA060`/`0x800CA120`), five GX state
//! blocks (`0x800CB8A0..0x800CC390`, including the no-argument background
//! variant), the mask-overlay record builders (`0x800CB470..0x800CCE00`,
//! `0x800CDED0`) and the message-record tail
//! (`0x800CE700..0x800CFCA0`). The public entry points are [`fn_800c10f0`],
//! [`fn_800cded0`], [`fn_800cb8a0`] and [`fn_800cdb30`]. The full table is in
//! `docs/COVERAGE_WAVE93_STAGE.md`.
//!
//! The wave-94 batch works the open entries of the `0x800B0000` bucket: the
//! actor bookkeeping layer between the course manager and the stage-object
//! sections. It adds the input record's full per-frame refresh
//! (`0x800B5C60`, which is also what fixes the field roles of the whole
//! cluster), its sprite angle and orientation counters
//! (`0x800B61A0`/`0x800B6250`/`0x800B6930`), the two sprite window tests
//! (`0x800B55F0`/`0x800B56E0`) and the aspect-ratio fix (`0x800B37E0`); the
//! timer record's start/step pair and its state chooser
//! (`0x800B8550`/`0x800B8EE0`/`0x800B8620`); the colour blocks of
