///   `li r6,2` / `lwz r12,r3+0x60` / `lfs f2,r4+0x10C` / `li r4,1` /
///   `lwz r12,r12+0x3FC` / `bcctr 20,0l`. The incoming `r3` is overwritten by
///   `mr r3,r4`, so the virtual receiver is `r4` and the incoming `f1` is
///   forwarded unchanged as the first float.
/// - observed: the virtual call is `(receiver, 1, 0, 2, f1, receiver[+0x10C])`;
///   afterwards `lwz r3,r13-0x5770` / `li r0,1` / `stw r0,r3+0x138` latches the
///   event flag.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `other`: the actor whose `+0x60` vtable supplies slot `+0x3FC`; its
///   `+0x10C` float becomes the second `f32` argument (the `r4` receiver).
/// - `value`: the incoming `f1`, forwarded unchanged as the first `f32`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One virtual call `(other, 1, 0, 2, value, other[+0x10C])`, then writes `1`
/// to `[r13-0x5770]+0x138` ([`W69_G_EVENT_STATE`]).
