/// Decodes the trigger record at `[this+0x10]` and optionally mirrors it.
///
/// The selector is again bit 0 of the record's first word, but the branches
/// differ from [`fn_80072db0`]: the square case repeats `+8` twice, and the
/// spanned case takes its third coordinate from `+0xC` before sorting `+4`
/// and `+8` into the first two slots. A non-zero `mirror` replaces the x
/// coordinate with `-x - 1.0f` (the `0x8042BC68` one).
