/// Probes the six-point ground block around the actor and publishes the
/// touched sides.
///
/// The grid record at `+0x10` supplies three column words; they are converted
/// and arranged into six points (three forward, three backward) around the
/// actor's `+0x14` position. Each point is probed with
/// [`W101_PROBE_CELL`]/[`W101_PROBE_KIND`], and a `0x400` reply sets the
/// point's mask word, the `+0xCC` state and, through the mask, the returned
/// bit word. The walk then re-tests every scroll-layer entry with
