/// Builds one BG tile map and fills it from the stage tile table.
///
/// The unit model is fetched through [`W101_BG_UNIT_MODEL`]; a `0x44`-byte
/// tile map is allocated and initialised, its bounds are read from the model,
/// and every cell is sampled with [`W101_TILE_PROBE`] and written back with
/// [`W101_TILE_WRITE`]. When the unit name is one of the three `Pa1_*` names,
/// tile ids `0x1A0..0x1A4`, `0x1B0..0x1B2` and `0x1C0..0x1C2` are remapped into
/// the two `+0x8F480` / `+0x8F930` effect lists before the tile is written.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80077eb0` at `0x80077EB0` (924 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80077eb0_FUN_80077eb0.c`
/// - observed: the `FUN_802b9240(0x44,...)` allocation, the
///   `FUN_80082410(iVar17,param_3,...,DAT_80377c48,uVar11 & 0xffff)` call, the
///   three `FUN_802e1ab4` string compares (`s_Pa1_nohara_8030f404`), the
///   `uVar16`/`uVar15` double loop and the two `+0x8F480`/`+0x8F930` block
///   writers.
/// - observed: the five GQR0 prologue `ldexpf` calls are dead.
/// - Removed: the modelled `_restgpr_20` epilogue call (`0x802DCDA4`).
///   it only restores registers.
///
