/// Steps a probe along a scroll-layer edge and keeps the highest contact.
///
/// The circle arm is the same test as [`fn_80073290`] but stores its angle at
/// `+0xC2` and subtracts the computed height from the entry's `+0x5C`. The flat
/// arm walks the edge chain: each step tests the current `x` through
/// `0x80080670`, selects the neighbouring edge row from the `0x802EF638` table
/// using the kind's `>> 14 & 3` group, derives the contact angle, and keeps the
/// smallest interpolated y seen (the loop advances the two-float cursor with
/// `0x8006D120` until it accepts the position).
