/// Forwards a cell request and returns the second word of the callee's pair.
///
/// `0x80077650` normalises the cell index and re-stores the tile id; it returns
/// its `r3`/`r4` pair, and this wrapper returns the low word (`r4`), which the
/// callers at `0x80070C60` and `0x801260F0` use as the test result.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80077700` at `0x80077700` (40 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/80077700_FUN_80077700.c`
/// - observed: `FUN_80077650(); return extraout_r4;`
/// - observed: the callers `FUN_80070c60` and `FUN_801260f0` pass
///   `(owner, x, y, mode)` and consume the returned word.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `this`: scene/owner forwarded to `0x80077650`.
/// - `x`, `y`: quantised cell coordinates.
/// - `mode`: forwarded test argument.
///
/// # Returns
/// The low word of the `0x80077650` result pair.
///
/// # Side effects
/// The callee updates the BG cell array and the tile masks.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this` must be a live scene object and the cell tables must be initialised.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the call, the returned register and all four argument names are
/// literal at the two call sites; the export itself prints the callee without
/// arguments.
pub unsafe fn fn_80077700(this: u32, x: u32, y: u32, mode: u32) -> u32 {
    let pair = w109_call4_u64(W109_CALL_80077650, this, x, y, mode);
    pair as u32
}

