// * `0x800A1830` `blr` at `0x800A1904` -> `0xD4 + 4 = 216` (the two 16-byte
//   stubs at `0x800A1908`/`0x800A190C` are the pad before `0x800A1910`);
// * `0x800A1980` `blr` at `0x800A19E0` -> `0x60 + 4 = 100`;
// * `0x800A2BE0` `blr` at `0x800A2BE8` -> `8 + 4 = 12`;
