/// Gates [`fn_800a2870`] on one `+0x1524` word of the actor's owner record.
///
/// The owner is reached as `*(*(actor + 8) + 4)`; its `+0x1524` word must be
/// non-zero before the predicate is asked. The three incoming registers are
/// forwarded unchanged: `r3` (the `context` of [`fn_800a2870`]), `r4` (the
/// actor) and `r5` (the mode), which Ghidra dropped from its prototype.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_800a2b20` at `0x800A2B20` (80 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/800a2b20_FUN_800a2b20.c`
/// - observed: `*(int *)(*(int *)(*(int *)(param_2 + 8) + 4) + 0x1524) != 0`
///   and the `FUN_800a2870()` call made with `r3`/`r4`/`r5` still live.
/// - extent: the `blr` sits at `0x800A2B6C` (76 bytes) with four bytes of
///   padding before `0x800A2B70`.
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `context`: forwarded to [`fn_800a2870`].
/// - `actor`: actor whose owner record is tested; also forwarded.
/// - `mode`: forwarded to [`fn_800a2870`].
///
/// # Returns
/// `1` when the owner word is set and the predicate answers non-zero, else `0`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Whatever [`fn_800a2870`] does.
///
/// # Safety
/// `actor`, `*(actor + 8)` and `*(*(actor + 8) + 4)` must be readable, and
/// whatever [`fn_800a2870`] needs must be live.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the word test and the call are literal; the three forwarded
/// arguments are read off the register file because the export prints none.
pub unsafe fn fn_800a2b20(context: u32, actor: usize, mode: u32) -> u32 {
    let owner = read_u32(read_u32(actor + 8) as usize + 4) as usize;
    if read_u32(owner + 0x1524) != 0 && fn_800a2870(context as usize, actor, mode) != 0 {
        1
    } else {
        0
    }
}

