///   = 112 bytes of code; the `functions.tsv` value of 116 also counts the
///   four zero bytes at `0x800AC384`, which belong to the following 4-byte
///   slot function at `0x800AC390`.
/// - correction: the export drops the second `0x8023A0B0` argument, but `r4`
///   is loaded at `0x800AC328` from `[[this + 0x758] + 0]` and is not touched
///   before the call; `0x8023A0B0` is the two-argument
///   `(holder, key)` lookup (`work/ghidra/main-gb/export/8023a0b0_...c`), so
///   the key is passed here.
/// - observed: the guard reads `r4 = [this + 0x758]` then `r4 = [r4 + 0]`, so
///   `+0x758` is a pointer to a record whose first word is the entry handle.
///
/// # Arguments
