///   `local_18[0] = FUN_8023a0b0(param_1 + 0x600,**(undefined4 **)(param_1 + 0x75c));`,
///   `FUN_801651f0(param_1 + 0x644,param_1 + 0x604,local_18,0);`,
///   `FUN_80169f80((double)*(float *)(unaff_r2 + -0x6c6c),param_1 + 0x604,param_1 + 0x644);`,
///   `FUN_801680e0((double)*(float *)(unaff_r2 + -0x6c70),param_1 + 0x644);`,
///   `(**(code **)(*(int *)(param_1 + 0x60) + 0x98))(param_1);`,
///   `FUN_8008c380(param_1 + 0x79c);`, then the four stores and
///   `*(uint *)(param_1 + 0x120) = *(uint *)(param_1 + 0x120) & 0xfffffff7;`.
/// - extent: `stwu r1,-0x20` at `0x800A_D090` through `bclr 20,0` at
///   `0x800A_D148` = `0xBC` = 188 bytes, exactly the `functions.tsv` size. The
///   four zero bytes at `0x800A_D14C`, the bare `bclr` at `0x800A_D150` and the
///   next zeros are alignment padding with no `functions.tsv` entry, and the
///   following listed body starts at `0x800A_DB00`.
/// - correction: `unaff_r2` is the small-data-2 base; the four literals are
///   `0x8042C414 = 0.0f`, `0x8042C410 = 1.0f`, `0x8042C45C = -0.275f` and
///   `0x8042C460 = 6.5f`.
