// Wave 229, lane A - the `0x80314534` object vtable (68 slots)
//
// ## What this batch is
//
// `0x80314534..0x80314644` is one contiguous 68-word array of code pointers
// (`word 68` at `0x80314644` is `0`, so the run ends exactly there). It is the
// virtual-method table of the actor class whose instance methods the wave-224
// and wave-225 lanes of this file already translate (`fn_800aade0`,
// `fn_800aa850`, `fn_800aa920`, `fn_800ab590`...). `docs/UNTABLED_POINTER_TABLES.md`
// ranks it 4 and counted 22 untabled entries / 3,584 B; that count is the set
// its prologue scan could see. A full sweep of the table finds **68 distinct
// targets and 65 untabled bodies totalling 4,268 B** - the doc's 22 (3,584 B
// exactly) plus 43 small stub slots it missed because they have no frame.
