//
// `0x80A0F610` (660 B) installs `0x803158D8` at `0x80A0F71C`, this table at
// `0x80A0F804`, and `0x80315770` at `0x80A0F83C`, so the small table is the
// middle layer of the big element. `0x80A70878` (500 B) installs `0x803158D8`
// at `0x80A70934` and this table last at `0x80A709EC`, so the same words are
// the final vtable of the small element. No other ELF names the header.
