///   `0x807B2300` and `0x807B9DDC` (the course-in reload `0x807B22E0` passes
///   `*(0x80377C48)` as the heap). No data word names it.
/// - Observed: `stwu r1,-0x10(r1)`; `mflr r0`; `stw r0,0x14(r1)`;
///   `stw r31,0xC(r1)`; `stw r30,0x8(r1)`; `bl 0x8016E4F0` (heap swap);
///   `mr r30,r3`; `li r3,0xEC0`; `bl 0x802B9210`; `cmpi cr0,0,r3,0`;
///   `mr r31,r3`; `41820024 bc 12,2` (`beq`, skip the build);
///   `lis r4,0x8009`; `lis r5,0x8009`; `addi r4,r4,-0x1470` (`0x8009EB90`);
///   `li r6,0x3B0`; `addi r5,r5,-0x1460` (`0x8009EBA0`); `li r7,4`;
///   `bl 0x802DC9A0`; `stw r31,-0x57E8(r13)`; restore `mr r3,r30`;
///   `bl 0x8016E4F0`; epilogue; `blr`.
/// - Table: the published array is [`G_STAGE_OBJECTS`] (`0x80429E98`), the base
///   walked by [`fn_8008ec40`].
///
/// # Arguments
/// - `heap`: heap selector installed for the allocation and restored afterwards.
///
/// # Returns
/// Nothing; the array pointer is published in [`G_STAGE_OBJECTS`].
///
/// # Side effects
/// Swaps the heap selector twice, allocates `0xEC0` bytes and constructs four
/// `0x3B0`-byte records.
///
/// # Safety
/// `heap` must be an allocator-accepted heap selector, and the constructor at
/// `0x8009EB90` must accept a zeroed `0x3B0`-byte element.
///
